    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (80.95) and **Seiya Suzuki** (75.03) anchoring our offensive output. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against M\u00e1rquez and a favorable order placement, though we remain vigilant regarding the 45% rain risk looming over **Seiya Suzuki**, whose high score is buoyed by a +16% park factor and an ideal stolen base environment against a slow delivery. **James Wood** (70.10) also demands attention; his elite 0.424 xwOBA and leadoff status against Imai make him a high-floor asset as he continues to drive our daily stolen base upside. We are prioritizing speed and matchup efficiency to navigate this rotation, ensuring that players like **Brice Turang** (61.87) and **Gabriel Moreno** (66.56) remain locked in against favorable SP_xERA figures.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Max Muncy** (44.60), who fell just shy of our starting threshold. While **Max Muncy** carries respectable power, the optimizer correctly favored the higher cumulative efficiency of our active lineup, specifically penalizing **Max Muncy** for a brutal matchup against Skubal\u2019s 2.74 xERA. We also gave consideration to **Austin Riley** (41.91) and **Isaac Paredes** (40.44), but both were ultimately pushed to the bench due to suboptimal SP matchups and lower projected efficiency scores compared to the flexibility offered by **Travis Bazzana** (53.42) and **Jose Caballero** (58.45). With **Cole Young** (37.18) falling well below our 40.0 floor, we are confident that our starting nine, including **Dalton Rushing**, **Josh Naylor**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Mickey Moniak**, provides the best strategic balance to maximize our 5x5 categorical output today.",
